# env — NEVER commit these. The repo is public.
.env
.env*.local
# ...and anything DERIVED from it. `.env*.local` matches `.env.local` but NOT
# `.env.local.sandbox-backup`, because the pattern requires the name to END in
# `.local`. A credentials backup made while switching environments slipped
# through that hole and was staged for a commit to a PUBLIC repo.
.env.local*
.env.production
!.env.example

